From 538dc8887c5c5074fc687d1610a1c84566263097 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:02:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(shared): K8 implementation diversity for the KDA
 route (lifecycle Level 3)

E3 rule K8: a verification bug in one ML-DSA library must not reach t+1
nodes. `K8Mode` is either `single:<impl>` (the deployment keeps each
implementation on at most t nodes, `k8_assignment_ok`) or
`agree:<impl>,<impl>` (two implementations must both accept; a
disagreement is refused and reported). With n = 13 and t = 4 the single
mode needs ceil(13/4) = 4 implementations, so four are wired, each behind
a feature: RustCrypto ml-dsa 0.1.1 (default), fips204 0.4.6, Cryspen
libcrux-ml-dsa 0.0.10 and PQClean's clean code via pqcrypto-mldsa 0.1.2.
None has been independently audited.

K7 vectors: every implementation passes NIST ACVP-Server ML-DSA sigVer
(FIPS 204, a7f283cd) on each interface it exposes, and all 631 C2SP
Wycheproof ML-DSA-44/65/87 verify vectors (20b25694); the pure interface
the route uses runs on all four. A test-only feature injects a fault
(one library accepts every well-sized signature) to show what each mode
lets through, on single nodes and on a 13-node assignment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
